  history: The USS Shenandoah was the first rigid airship built by the United States
    Navy, as the reconnaissance airship and technology testbed, completed in 1923.
    It was the first hellium-filled rigid airship and the first of its kind to fly
    across North America. She was destroyed in a storm over Ohio on September 3,
    1925.
